{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Patel. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can I confirm your name and date of birth?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m Sarah Chen. My birthday is March 12, 2130."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thank you, Sarah. I see you’ve come in for worsening shortness of breath and to evaluate your tracheostomy. You’ve had this tube since you were three months old, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, since I was a baby. I was born early, at 26 weeks, and my lungs never fully developed. I’ve had trouble breathing my whole life."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right, bronchopulmonary dysplasia from prematurity. And you’ve had four airway surgeries already?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, the last one was when I was about ten. They tried to remove the trach a few times, but I couldn’t breathe without it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Lately, you’ve been more short of breath, even at rest, and your cough has been worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s harder to do simple things like walking to the bathroom. And my sputum is sometimes green, but no fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. We’re planning a rigid bronchoscopy today to look at your airway and possibly change your trach tube."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I be asleep for that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’ll be under general anesthesia. The new tube will be fenestrated and uncuffed—Portex size 7 mm inside. That may help with speaking and airflow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I hope it helps me breathe easier. I’m tired of feeling so winded."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2161-01-11 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do our best. After the procedure, you’ll go to recovery, then back here to the floor. Your vitals look stable now—98% on room air."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2161-01-11 15:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Sarah, you’re back from the OR. The bronchoscopy went well. We replaced your trach tube successfully and extubated you in the OR."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2161-01-11 15:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good. I don’t remember much. Does it feel different?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2161-01-11 15:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Too early to tell, but the airway looked better. We’ll keep monitoring. You’ll continue your nebulizers and pulmonary toilet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Sarah. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My throat feels really sore, and my voice is super hoarse. I can barely talk."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s not uncommon after the procedure. We’re concerned about some swelling in your voice box. We may need a flexible bronchoscopy to check it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Swelling? Is that serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s manageable. We’ll do the scope tomorrow to get a better look. In the meantime, try to rest your voice as much as possible."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try not to talk much. But what’s causing the swelling?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Could be irritation from the tube or an infection. We’re starting you on fluconazole just in case it’s a fungal infection—thrush in the larynx."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, like a yeast infection in the throat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2161-01-12 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. It’s more common in people with chronic airway issues. We’ll treat it for 14 days to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2161-01-12 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also started a higher dose of omeprazole. Your GERD might be contributing to the throat irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2161-01-12 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had heartburn for years. Does that really affect my airway?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2161-01-12 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, stomach acid can reflux up and irritate your larynx, especially when lying down. That’s why we want you to sit up during meals and keep your head elevated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2161-01-12 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll make sure to do that at home too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2161-01-13 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Sarah. Ready for the flexible bronchoscopy this afternoon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2161-01-13 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I guess so. Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2161-01-13 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get sedation, so you’ll be relaxed. It’s to check the swelling we’re worried about—supraglottic edema."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2161-01-13 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi Sarah, back from the scope. We saw significant swelling in your upper airway and signs of laryngitis. No obstruction, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2161-01-13 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what does that mean? Is it dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2161-01-13 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. It explains your hoarseness. We’ll keep you on fluconazole and voice rest. The swelling should improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2161-01-13 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I ever get my voice back fully?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2161-01-13 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most likely, yes. It just takes time and rest. We’ll monitor closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2161-01-14 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news, Sarah. Your voice is already a little stronger today. The swelling is starting to go down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2161-01-14 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried I’d lose my voice for good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2161-01-14 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also consulting thoracic surgery. They want to explore long-term options for your bronchopulmonary dysplasia—maybe a stent trial or more tests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2161-01-14 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "More surgery? I’ve already had so many."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2161-01-14 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not right now. They’re just gathering info—pH testing for reflux, questionnaires. Nothing urgent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2161-01-14 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well overall. We think you can go home tomorrow if your breathing stays stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2161-01-14 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. I miss my mom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2161-01-14 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send you home with instructions: trach care as before, humidified air, and finish the full 14-day fluconazole course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2161-01-14 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the lozenges for my throat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2161-01-14 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, menthol lozenges as needed. And liquid Tylenol for pain. No solid food for now—stick to soft or liquid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning, Sarah. You’re cleared to go home. Your breathing is stable, and your voice is improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I feel a lot better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Remember: head of bed elevated, sit up for meals, and follow up with your pulmonologist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. And finish all my meds, especially the fluconazole."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Take care, Sarah. Call if you have trouble breathing or your voice worsens."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again, Dr. Patel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Have a safe trip home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad this is over. But I hope I don’t have to come back soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll do our best to keep you stable. Your team will coordinate the next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take your albuterol and acetylcysteine nebs as prescribed. And montelukast twice daily now—chewable tablets."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. The dose changed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we increased it to better control your asthma symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to take it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "And the omeprazole twice daily now—to protect your throat from acid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll set reminders. Don’t want another flare-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Smart plan. We’re here if you need us."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Dr. Patel. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great, Sarah. Keep up the good work."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2161-01-15 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you at follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2161-01-11 14:20:00",
    "admission_end": "2161-01-15 11:40:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 31-year-old woman with a history of bronchopulmonary dysplasia from prematurity and chronic tracheostomy was admitted for progressive dyspnea and evaluation of her airway. She underwent a rigid bronchoscopy with replacement of her tracheostomy tube to a fenestrated, uncuffed Portex tube. Postoperatively, she developed hoarseness and was found to have supraglottic edema and laryngitis, likely fungal (laryngeal thrush), for which she was started on fluconazole. GERD management was intensified with omeprazole. Her voice improved with rest, and she was discharged home on day four with instructions to continue trach care, complete the antifungal course, and follow up as an outpatient. Thoracic surgery recommended further work-up for long-term management.",
    "problems": [
      "Other tracheostomy complications",
      "Other candidiasis of other specified sites",
      "Edema of larynx",
      "Acute laryngitis without mention of obstruction",
      "Chronic obstructive asthma, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
